## 5. Login Page Design

![Login page](file:///C:/Users/malik/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c61c8478-758a-4daa-a212-2917ccb2149b/login_page_final_1771602338187.png)

What makes it elegant:

- **Minimal card** — no visible card border, content floats on the gradient background
- **Logo component** — centered above inputs, acts as branding anchor
- **Input styling** — `login-input` class: clean, generous padding, rounded corners
- **Primary CTA** — full-width solid button (`login-button`)
- **Divider pattern** — `"oder"` label flanked by `flex: 1` lines (`::before`/`::after` pseudo-elements with `var(--color-border)` background)
- **Secondary SSO button** — `btn-modern btn-secondary` with left-aligned logo icon, full-width
- **Auth footer** — register link in muted color below form
- **Vertical centering** — ghost element technique ensures card stays truly centered even with footer

---

## 6. Settings Page Design

What makes it clean:

- **Modern card system** — `.modern-card` with `.modern-card-header` + `.modern-card-body`
- **Grouped fields** — FieldRegistry groups, each card has a colored icon badge (8×8 → `bg-{color}-100`, `text-{color}-600`)
- **Auto-save pattern** — `data-save-mode="auto"`, no submit button. Save indicator is a fixed pill (`bottom: 16px; right: 16px`) with `.saving` / `.success` / `.error` states
- **Field types**: text inputs (`form-input-modern`), toggles (`modern-checkbox`), secrets (password + eye toggle inline)
- **Danger zone** — separate `.modern-card-danger` with red icon badge and destructive `btn-danger` button
- **Delete confirmation** — multi-step SweetAlert2 flow: warning → name-type confirmation → loading spinner overlay

---

## 7. Rehearsal Card Design (Meine Meldungen)

The core interaction pattern of the app. What makes it work:

| Element | Technique |
|---|---|
| **Card** | `border-left: 4px` color-coded by status (green/red/gray). Rounded with `--radius-lg`, `--shadow-sm` |
| **Weekday** | Bold 24 px gradient-clipped text (`-webkit-background-clip: text`) with underline `::after` pseudo-element |
| **Time display** | Monospace font `'Kantumruy Pro'` + dynamic `scaleX()` stretch to match date width |
| **Badges** | 10 px uppercase, `letter-spacing: 0.3px`, pill-shaped: type badge (purple tint), section badge (gray tint), emoji badges |
| **Action buttons** | 52 × 52 px, `border-radius: --radius-lg`, two states: **selected** (color gradient bg + colored shadow) and **deselected** (opacity 0.4, grayscale icon filter) |
| **Deselected hover** | Gradual opacity restore (0.7), slight `translateY(-1px)` lift, filter desaturate halfway |
| **Note tag** | Quote icon + italic text in muted colors, appended at bottom of card |
| **Long-press reset** | 500 ms hold → resets to neutral state with toast feedback |
| **Update queue** | Debounced AJAX with save indicator overlay. Prevents double-submit and page-leave during save |

### Container Entrance Animation
```css
.container-app {
  opacity: 0;
  transform: translateY(8px);
  transition: opacity 0.4s ease-out, transform 0.4s ease-out;
}
```
Content fades in and slides up on mount → premium feel.

---

## 8. Universal Design Principles (Extracted)

### Gradients as Depth, Not Decoration
Every gradient serves hierarchy: cards lift off backgrounds, buttons signal interactivity, active states glow. Never use gradients purely for color — they always communicate z-depth or emphasis.

### Micro-animations Everywhere
- `transition: all var(--transition-base)` on interactive elements
- `translateY(-1px)` on hover/active for tactile "lift"
- `scaleX` stretch for typography alignment
- `transform: scale(0.95)` on `:active` for press feedback
- Fade-in entrance animations for page content

### Color to Communicate State
Three-color system is universal: green = positive/attending, red = negative/not-attending, gray = neutral/pending. This applies in sidebar stats bar, rehearsal cards, dashboard charts, and tree-view status icons.

### Progressive Disclosure
- Sidebar stats show high-level bar → details on hover/click
- Rehearsal cards show summary → expand for schedule timeline
- Dashboard tree-view: collapsible sections with chevron rotation
- Danger zone: multi-step confirmation with escalating seriousness

### Whitespace as Feature
- Generous padding (`--space-3` to `--space-8`) in all containers
- `gap` for flexbox spacing instead of margins → uniform rhythm
- Cards have both header and body padding for clear visual separation

### Component Encapsulation
Each component carries its own `<style>` block with scoped CSS. Styles use CSS custom properties from the theme, making all components automatically theme-aware. Pattern:
```php
<?php $renderComponent = false; include 'component.php'; ?> <!-- styles only -->
<?php $renderComponent = true; include 'component.php'; ?>  <!-- full render -->
```

### Semantic Class Names
- `.modern-card`, `.modern-card-header`, `.modern-card-body`
- `.sidebar-nav-link.active`, `.rehearsal-card.status-attending`
- `.btn-modern.btn-primary`, `.btn-modern.btn-danger`
- State classes: `.selected`, `.deselected`, `.disabled`, `.loading`

---

## 9. Quick Reference: Building a New Component

1. **Create** `src/Views/components/my-component.php`
2. **Embed styles** in a `<style>` block at the top, using only `var(--token)` values
3. **Support** `$renderComponent` flag for styles-only inclusion
4. **Use** existing patterns: `.modern-card` for card layout, `.btn-modern` for buttons, `.form-input-modern` for inputs
5. **Apply** entrance animations via `.container-app` wrapper
6. **Add** hover/active micro-animations: `translateY(-1px)`, opacity transitions, gradient shifts
7. **Use** status coding: green/red/gray for tri-state data
8. **Test** in dark mode — if you only used tokens, it should just work
